From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Doors <doors@localhost>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: dts: rm69a10-hdmi: the board's own tree with the
 LT9611 in place of the panel

Applies on top of the LILYGO BSP stack (after 0062 and 0064) and Doors
0070-0074. Doors-owned; see docs/decisions/ADR-011-kernel-patches.md and
docs/hardware/HDMI_OUTPUT.md in the Doors repository.

BSP patch 0062 made k230-canmv-rm69a10-hdmi.dts an include of the SDK's
k230-canmv-v3.dts, a CanMV-K230 board description. On the T-Display K230
that tree drives the LT9611 (HDMI_GATE.md rounds 1-6) but it has no
camera sensor node, no I2C4 or MCLK1 pin set-up for the sensor, spi0 (LoRa)
and uart1 (nRF52840) disabled, no BOOT key and an 8-bit eMMC description of
the SDIO Wi-Fi slot (DOCUMENTED: decompiled DTB, sha256 2a6b49ad..., the
same on every Doors image and VERIFIED on unit B 2026-10-10). So an HDMI
boot loses the camera and the radio, which no userspace change can bring
back.

This makes the HDMI tree the board's own panel tree with exactly three
changes, so the camera, LoRa, the nRF52840 link, the keyboard base's pin
set-up, the BOOT key, Wi-Fi and the memory map are those of a panel boot:

- the RM69A10 panel node is deleted and the DSI host's port 1 endpoint is
  wired to the LT9611 (the panel and the bridge share the DSI lanes on this
  board; canaan_dsi takes whichever device is on port 1);
- the GT9895 touch node is deleted and the LT9611 added on i2c3 @0x3b,
  reset GPIO24, interrupt GPIO23 falling, with the hdmi-connector node. The
  touch controller and the bridge share GPIO23 and GPIO24 on the board
  (schematic sheet 7), so only one can have a driver. Bridge and connector
  nodes as in the SDK's k230-canmv-v3.dts;
- canaan,skip-fbdev-setup is deleted, so fbdev emulation runs as it did
  with the vendor HDMI tree the gate proved.

The decompiled DTB differs from the panel tree's in exactly those nodes,
the model string and the phandle numbering. The panel tree
(k230-canmv-rm69a10.dts) is not changed. The vendor's #if 0 reference block
in this file is kept as it was.

Signed-off-by: Doors <doors@localhost>
---
 arch/riscv/boot/dts/canaan/k230-canmv-rm69a10-hdmi.dts | 90 ++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 85 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/canaan/k230-canmv-rm69a10-hdmi.dts
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/canaan/k230-canmv-rm69a10-hdmi.dts
@@ -221,10 +221,90 @@
 #endif
 
 /*
- * The board-specific HDMI attempt above is kept for reference but is not used.
- * The SDK CanMV v3 HDMI DTB was verified on T-Display K230: LT9611 probes,
- * EDID is read, and HDMI-A-1 exposes 800x480@60. Reuse that known-good HDMI
- * graph until a reduced board-specific DTS is proven.
+ * Doors: the LILYGO T-Display K230 with its display output on the LT9611
+ * DSI-to-HDMI bridge instead of the RM69A10 AMOLED.
+ *
+ * This is the board's own panel tree (k230-canmv-rm69a10.dts, with every
+ * BSP and Doors change to it) with exactly three things changed, so an HDMI
+ * boot keeps the camera, LoRa, the nRF52840 link, the keyboard base, the
+ * BOOT key, the SDIO Wi-Fi and the memory map of a panel boot:
+ *
+ *  - the RM69A10 panel is removed and the DSI host's output port is wired
+ *    to the bridge (the panel and the bridge share the DSI lanes; the DSI
+ *    driver takes whichever device is on port 1);
+ *  - the GT9895 touch controller is removed and the LT9611 is added on the
+ *    same bus (i2c3 @0x3b). They share reset GPIO24 and interrupt GPIO23 on
+ *    the board, so only one of them can have a driver;
+ *  - fbdev emulation is enabled again, as in the vendor HDMI tree that the
+ *    Doors HDMI gate proved (the panel tree skips it to keep the U-Boot
+ *    splash on the AMOLED).
+ *
+ * The bridge and connector nodes are the SDK's k230-canmv-v3.dts ones.
+ * Doors-owned; see docs/hardware/HDMI_OUTPUT.md in the Doors repository.
  */
+#include "k230-canmv-rm69a10.dts"
 
-#include "k230-canmv-v3.dts"
+/ {
+	model = "Canaan CanMV-K230 with LT9611 HDMI";
+
+	hdmi: connector {
+		compatible = "hdmi-connector";
+		label = "hdmi";
+		type = "a";
+
+		port {
+			hdmi_connector_in: endpoint {
+				remote-endpoint = <&lt9611_out>;
+			};
+		};
+	};
+};
+
+&display {
+	/delete-property/ canaan,skip-fbdev-setup;
+};
+
+&dsi {
+	/delete-node/ panel@0;
+
+	ports {
+		port@1 {
+			/delete-node/ endpoint;
+
+			dsi_out_lt9611: endpoint {
+				remote-endpoint = <&lt9611_in>;
+			};
+		};
+	};
+};
+
+&i2c3 {
+	/delete-node/ gt9895@5d;
+
+	lt9611: hdmi-bridge@3b {
+		compatible = "lontium,lt9611";
+		reg = <0x3b>;
+		reset-gpios = <&gpio0_ports 24 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		interrupt-parent = <&gpio0_ports>;
+		interrupts = <23 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_FALLING>;
+
+		ports {
+			#address-cells = <1>;
+			#size-cells = <0>;
+
+			port@1 {
+				reg = <1>;
+				lt9611_in: endpoint {
+					remote-endpoint = <&dsi_out_lt9611>;
+				};
+			};
+
+			port@2 {
+				reg = <2>;
+				lt9611_out: endpoint {
+					remote-endpoint = <&hdmi_connector_in>;
+				};
+			};
+		};
+	};
+};
